        "original_id": "516c3e85-f6c3-588a-9598-018c0c97e0ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: opéra comique\n- Places: Paris theatre\n- Works: Carmen, Aida, novella Carmen\n- People: Georges Bizet, Henri Meilhac, Ludovic Halévy, Prosper Mérimée, Nell Rankin, Giuseppe Verdi\n- Roles: Amneris\n\nFacts:\n- The concept of opéra comique is associated with a Paris theatre of the same name.\n- The concept of opéra comique is not always comic or light in nature.\n- The work Carmen is perhaps the most famous opéra comique, and Carmen is a tragedy.\n- Prosper Mérimée wrote the novella Carmen.\n- Georges Bizet composed Carmen as an opera in four acts.\n- Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy wrote the libretto for Carmen based on Prosper Mérimée's novella of the same title.\n- Giuseppe Verdi composed Aida.\n- Nell Rankin was particularly admired for her portrayals of Amneris in Aida and the title role in Carmen.",
